iscovered follow-up work has a first-class destination: phase [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]agents record PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP notes, land agents file them as [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]task beads and mark them ready, a builtin chop raises a per-bead [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]triage gate whose default action launches a detached #bd/work_task [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]agent, and the task type and ready status render beautifully on [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]every bead surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_beads.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]202607/prompts/task_beads.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-bg[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-bg/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core task type, ready status, and ready-query [/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]redefinition[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-model: add IssueTypeWire::Task and StatusWire::Ready with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validation, schema CHECKs and migrations, redefine the ready query to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unblocked ready task beads, extend CLI parse/render/stats tables, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cover with parity and mutation tests in the sase-core linked repo.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python model mirror, parsers, and CLI text[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py-model: mirror the task type and ready status through model.py, db.py [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrations, jsonl/wire, parse_type_arg, argparse choices, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ready/stats/detail handlers, doctor branches, and the sase-core-rs pin.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared bead type and ready status presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]presentation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation: create bead_type_presentation.py as the single type [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph/accent/chip authority, add the ready row to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BEAD_STATUS_PRESENTATIONS, and extend the exhaustive presentation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE TUI task surfaces and PNG goldens[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui: add a Tasks section and task row kind to the Plans pane with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]filters and detail chips, make the agents-pane bead lane and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan-association role type-aware, extend the bead autocomplete and edit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal, and regenerate PNG snapshot goldens with open and ready task [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixtures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bead pages, mobile wire, and remaining text surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pages-mobile[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pages-mobile: render the task type and ready status on published bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pages, admit task in the mobile bead type filters, and sweep remaining [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]issue_type branches for task-awareness.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove bd/next, rewire capture, add bd/work_task[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]xprompts[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]xprompts: delete the bd/next xprompt and its doc/test references, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redirect bd/work_phase_bead to PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP notes, teach [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bd/land_epic to file ready task beads, and add the bd/work_task xprompt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with its tag, resolver, and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase bead work for task beads and detached submitter[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]task-launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-model, xprompts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-launch: route task bead targets through sase bead work with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]single-commit in-progress marking, rollback, dry-run, model routing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including a task_worker alias, single-segment prompt composition ending [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in bd/work_task, and a task_launch.py detached submitter mirroring [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic_launch.py.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TaskTriage gate kind end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]triage-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after task-launch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage-gate: register a task_triage gate kind with launch-default and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]close-with-reason branches, build the spec and command shims in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task_gate.py, implement apply_side_effects to submit the detached launch[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or close with the feedback reason, and wire ACE and mobile surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bead_task_triage builtin chop[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]triage-chop[dim] · [dim][/dim]after triage-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage-chop: add the bead_task_triage chop to the checks lumberjack lane[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with per-bead gate creation, stale-gate cancellation, state-file dedupe,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]counters, tests, and axe docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory template, sase_beads skill, and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-memory-skill[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui, pages-mobile, triage-chop[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-memory-skill: append the user-authorized task-bead recommendation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the builtin memory template and regenerate via sase memory init, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the sase_beads generated-skill source, and document the type, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]status, gate, and chop in docs/beads.md and docs/notifications.md.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-bg","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-bg.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-08baec1ec592cf967365a032a7283367","started_at":"2026-07-30T22:57:21.959851+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"298b0781530e60877efe49b28287452d4fccd8a7b56ab99eca6619cc9b6f79f8","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bg.9/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"5b6a024199e2dc407df38762df88536896dfd2bf2cda4017819bcb76124d6f65","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bg.9/meta.json","size_bytes":603},"prompt":{"digest":"c9c6dc04809526fd911560df197d806e57124acddb3fc622fdbe098c3d818f56","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bg.9/prompt.md","size_bytes":154},"state":{"digest":"5b93b87a5c229a62626d7e0efac372887351f344305544e9d6adc055f8678dec","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bg.9/state.json","size_bytes":